[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2638284370","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101770#issuecomment-2638284370","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101770","id":2638284370,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6dQQZS","user":{"login":"deralmas","id":31065808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMDY1ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31065808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas","html_url":"https://github.com/deralmas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-05T23:43:29Z","updated_at":"2025-02-05T23:43:29Z","body":"Hi, thank you for the report! I'm not really sure what could have caused the behavior you're seeing, especially when running from vscode.\n\nCould you please send me a complete debug log? You can generate it like so:\n\n`WAYLAND_DEBUG=1 insert-path-to-godot-here --verbose > wayland.log 2>&1`","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2638284370/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2660359298","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101770#issuecomment-2660359298","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101770","id":2660359298,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ekdyC","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-14T22:07:11Z","updated_at":"2025-02-14T22:07:11Z","body":"I've never used Hyprland so I'm not sure how to test this effectively, but I installed it on Fedora 41 and gave it a quick try.\n\nIt spammed me with a blinking toast that I'm using a default config instead of a custom one, and apparently that's not ok... but launching kitty and starting godot from the command line seemed to work fine. The font rendering seemed glitchy but functional.\n\nSo I suspect that your Hyprland config is relevant to reproduce the issue.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2660359298/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2660417538","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101770#issuecomment-2660417538","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101770","id":2660417538,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6eksAC","user":{"login":"Nikitf777","id":127026067,"node_id":"U_kgDOB5JDkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/127026067?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nikitf777","html_url":"https://github.com/Nikitf777","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nikitf777/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nikitf777/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nikitf777/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nikitf777/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nikitf777/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nikitf777/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nikitf777/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nikitf777/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nikitf777/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-14T22:44:12Z","updated_at":"2025-02-15T09:24:48Z","body":"> So I suspect that your Hyprland config is relevant to reproduce the issue.\n\nI don't think it's just a config issue. As I said above, for me it's more likely an Hyprland/XWayland issue, as enabling \"prefer Wayland\" fixes it. Also I tested it again today and launching from VSCode doesn't work again (I don't know why it DID work at first. Maybe it was actually a 4.3 build, but it's very unlikely, because I tested it many times). I also noticed that sometimes the window appears if you are clicking fast and launching the executable many times. So the only remaining questions are why the Editor works while the project manager doesn't and why 4.3 branch has no such issues. Are there any changes in the area of display managers from 4.3 to 4.4?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2660417538/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2660631916","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101770#issuecomment-2660631916","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101770","id":2660631916,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6elgVs","user":{"login":"deralmas","id":31065808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMDY1ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31065808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas","html_url":"https://github.com/deralmas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-15T02:04:31Z","updated_at":"2025-02-15T02:04:31Z","body":"> As I said above, for me it's now likely an Hyprland/XWayland issue, as enabling \"prefer Wayland\" fixes it.\n\nOh that changes a things a lot. XWayland is known to have lots of weird quirks (see #88346). This is also not the first weird XWayland-related issue that happens on hyprland (like #96137).\n\nI am unfortunately not very experienced with the X11 backend; I work mainly on native Wayland support, so I'll unassign myself from this issue. I think that this can be very probably worked around but I have no idea how.\n\nIn the meantime, as you might have noticed, native Wayland might be a reasonable workaround, although please bear in mind that it's experimental and WIP - it still misses some features.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2660631916/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2660891966","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101770#issuecomment-2660891966","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101770","id":2660891966,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6emf0-","user":{"login":"Nikitf777","id":127026067,"node_id":"U_kgDOB5JDkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/127026067?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nikitf777","html_url":"https://github.com/Nikitf777","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nikitf777/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nikitf777/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nikitf777/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nikitf777/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nikitf777/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nikitf777/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nikitf777/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nikitf777/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nikitf777/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-15T12:07:51Z","updated_at":"2025-02-15T12:50:20Z","body":"Small but important update: I found the exact commit from which the issue begins to occur: 9d0c41a. On the previous commit, 0ed2cb0, there are no problems.\nVideo:\n(I wanted to attach it as a file but it was always failed to upload)\nhttps://youtu.be/DDYrZIElKuI","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2660891966/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2660921705","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101770#issuecomment-2660921705","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101770","id":2660921705,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6emnFp","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-15T13:13:38Z","updated_at":"2025-02-15T13:13:38Z","body":"Did you use `git bisect` to find that? See [bisecting regressions](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/contributing/workflow/bisecting_regressions.html).\n\nThere's no way for 9d0c41a to be the cause of this issue, it's only modifying IDE configuration files for people editing Godot source code, there's no impact on the compilation and behavior of Godot itself.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2660921705/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2660930986","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101770#issuecomment-2660930986","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101770","id":2660930986,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6empWq","user":{"login":"Nikitf777","id":127026067,"node_id":"U_kgDOB5JDkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/127026067?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nikitf777","html_url":"https://github.com/Nikitf777","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nikitf777/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nikitf777/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nikitf777/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nikitf777/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nikitf777/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nikitf777/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nikitf777/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nikitf777/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nikitf777/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-15T13:42:58Z","updated_at":"2025-02-15T15:15:49Z","body":"> Did you use `git bisect` to find that?\n\nIsn't the `git checkout` command enough for this?\n\n> there's no impact on the compilation and behavior of Godot itself\n\nTechnically there is. At least it changes the commit id shown at the bottom right corner of the project manager (watch the video).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2660930986/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2660947099","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101770#issuecomment-2660947099","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101770","id":2660947099,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6emtSb","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-15T14:26:45Z","updated_at":"2025-02-15T14:26:45Z","body":"> > Did you use `git bisect` to find that?\n> \n> Isn't the `git checkout` command enough for this?\n\nIt can, if you know very well how to do a binary search on a non linear Git graph. `git bisect` does that for you and avoids the risk of making assumptions from the order of commits in `git log` which is influenced by merge commits to reconcile disjoint branch histories.\n\nFor example here, the commit you identified as causing the regression has this metadata:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3ab11545-42c3-4ffa-9b8c-a1db6a498f0e)\n\nThe parent commit is not the one you identified above. You can only reliably compare merge commits if you're eyeballing when they got merged, but the actual commit implementing the changes might be based on an older history, so when you test them you can be misled.\n\n> > there's no impact on the compilation and behavior of Godot itself\n> \n> Technically there is. At least it changes the commit id shown at the bottom left corner of the project manager (watch the video).\n\nFair enough, but that has no impact on the behavior of Godot. If it did, I'd suggest you might be having memory corruption on your system.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2660947099/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2660950439","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101770#issuecomment-2660950439","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101770","id":2660950439,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6emuGn","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-15T14:36:19Z","updated_at":"2025-02-15T14:36:19Z","body":"The \"eyeballed\" binary search you did is useful still though, it gives you narrow bounds for a git bisect to find the actual merge that caused the issue.\n\nYou can do it with:\n```\ngit bisect start\ngit bisect good 0ed2cb0\ngit bisect bad 9d0c41a\n```\n\nIf I'm right, there should be some steps to test between the two identified by git bisect (not on PC now to confirm). If it fails because the branches can't be reconciled, then I'd suggest backing a bit in the history, picking a **merge commit** from e.g. Jan 9 (assumed `good`, but worth testing first to confirm) and another one from Jan 14 (assumed `bad`, likewise test to be sure).","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2660950439/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2661630816","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101770#issuecomment-2661630816","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101770","id":2661630816,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6epUNg","user":{"login":"Nikitf777","id":127026067,"node_id":"U_kgDOB5JDkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/127026067?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/us